<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aberdyfi</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Aberdovey</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aberdyfi is a village at the mouth of the Dyfi on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cardigan-bay">Cardigan Bay</a> in Gwynedd, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>. In 1216 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llywelyn-the-great">Llywelyn the Great</a> held an assembly there at which he divided the lands of Deheubarth among its princes and the other Welsh rulers acknowledged his supremacy, a high point of the native principality.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aberdyfi.jpg" alt="Aberdyfi" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jrfw51 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aberdyfi_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
